      "widgets_values": [
        "Live-action, 1990s Hong Kong arthouse film, low-key night interior, visible 35mm film grain, shallow depth of field: everything more than one metre behind the table is heavily blurred, only the speaking face is sharp. The room sits mostly in shadow. A warm amber tungsten pool falls on the formica table and on skin; the walls fall to deep teal-green; red and green neon from the street outside bleeds through rain-streaked glass and rims the women's hair with cold color. Rain is clearly visible running down the glass for the whole shot. Foreground haze from a hot water kettle drifts across the lower frame. The two women sit in the lower third of the frame with dark empty space above them.\n\n[Shot 1] A medium two-shot across the table, camera low and slightly off-axis. On the left, Lin: glossy dark-red lipstick, voluminous side-parted black waves, pearl drop earrings, a dark green silk qipao with a high collar. On the right, Su: no makeup, damp shoulder-length black hair tucked behind one ear, a loose white cotton shirt, a thin silver chain. Both sit still, only small head movements. Lin stirs a cup of coffee without looking up; Su watches the rain on the glass, then turns her eyes back to Lin. A radio behind the counter plays a faint, muffled Cantonese ballad. The camera pushes in with very small amplitude at slow speed. Neither speaks.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.800, the camera cuts to an over-the-shoulder shot from behind Lin's left shoulder: her dark green silk shoulder is soft and out of focus in the left foreground, occupying about a quarter of the frame, and Su's face is the only sharp element across the table. Su (S1), a late-twenties East Asian woman with a bare face and damp black hair, holds Lin's gaze and says in a low, level voice: <d>[Chinese] 雨停之前，你会说真话吗？</d> Her fingertips stop on the rim of her glass. The line finishes by 00:06.800; after that she closes her mouth and stays silent for the rest of the shot. Lin does not speak; her lips stay still. The camera holds a static shot.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:08.200, the shot cuts to the reverse over-the-shoulder from behind Su's right shoulder: her white cotton collar and damp hair fill the near-right foreground, soft and out of focus, and Lin's face is the only sharp element across the table. Lin (S2), the woman with dark-red lipstick and pearl earrings, lowers her eyes to the coffee cup first, then lifts them to Su and says in a quiet, unhurried voice: <d>[Chinese] 真话我早说了——是你没在听。</d> The line finishes by 00:11.800; she then holds Su's gaze in silence. Su does not speak; her lips stay still. The camera pushes in with very small amplitude at slow speed and comes to rest on Lin's eyes, holding until the 14.4-second mark.\n\nEach line is spoken exactly once, with no repeated syllables and no trailing vocal after it. Both women keep the same hairstyle, clothing, makeup and jewelry in every shot. Same room, same table, same lighting. No on-screen text, no subtitles, no watermark.\n\noverall_soundscape: Steady rain drums on the window glass and drips into a metal awning outside. A ceiling fan turns overhead with a soft, even hum. A ceramic spoon clicks against a cup, a chair leg scrapes the tiled floor, and a distant radio plays a muffled Cantonese ballad behind the counter. Traffic passes in the wet street without ever becoming clear.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A muted trumpet and upright bass play a slow, sparse jazz phrase at low volume, with one sustained string note held under the last shot and fading out as the image ends.",
